-- examples/checks/demand-depth-wall.rofl — demand_depth_wall: SIX HUNDRED CALLS DEEP,
-- EACH OF ANOTHER KEY, END AT THE DEPTH WALL in both engines, never at the stack of
-- the host (the review of 13a742e: each call answered on demand held more of the
-- stack, and the TypeScript engine died of "Maximum call stack size exceeded" where
-- it had stopped at budget,spent(depth,513,512); the frames held through each call are
-- kept small, f_a_cycle_of_open_calls_iterated_call_by_call). dd_c leaves W open, so
-- it is answered on demand, each call from the next node.
